Package: PEPI
Type: Package
Title: PEPI - Quantifying Epigenetic Dynamics from Genomics Data
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Riccardo", "Bergamin", email = "rbergamin@units.it", role=c("aut","cre")),
    person("Giulio", "Caravagna", email = "gcaravagn@gmail.com", role=c("ctb")),
    person("Clara", "Canavese", email = "arnold@sissa.com", role=c("ctb")))
Maintainer: Riccardo Bergamin <rbergamin@units.it>
Description: PEPI is a package implementing a Bayesian framework for studying epigenetic dynamics from longitudinal genomics data. It combines variant allele frequencies (VAFs) from sorted positive (⊕) and negative (⊖) cells with longitudinal cell counts to infer clade-level dynamics, epigenetic switching rates, and the impact of driver mutations.
